1
00:00:01,207 --> 00:00:02,680
Hey...

2
00:00:07,915 --> 00:00:10,060
I can say this now, but...

3
00:00:13,214 --> 00:00:14,587
I...

4
00:00:17,987 --> 00:00:19,991
I really...

5
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,620
respect you.

6
00:00:25,073 --> 00:00:26,702
You respect me?

7
00:00:27,956 --> 00:00:31,884
Like how you came back
even though you had plans.

8
00:00:31,884 --> 00:00:35,108
Well, that's because I'm also
part of the team.

9
00:00:35,108 --> 00:00:37,715
You stick to your ideals,

10
00:00:37,715 --> 00:00:41,294
regardless of how it looks to others.

11
00:00:41,294 --> 00:00:44,484
You're able to take action for other people.

12
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,808
I respect that.

13
00:00:51,182 --> 00:00:52,657
Do you really?

14
00:00:52,657 --> 00:00:54,090
I do.

15
00:00:55,896 --> 00:00:57,371
Well...

16
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:00,110
Thank you.

17
00:01:00,110 --> 00:01:01,530
Not at all.

18
00:01:04,823 --> 00:01:07,624
Hey, about this page here...

19
00:01:07,624 --> 00:01:10,663
Did the last point person share it?

20
00:01:10,663 --> 00:01:13,156
Probably not yet.

21
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:33,872
[Sorry for leaving so suddenly today.
I'm done with work.]

22
00:01:37,577 --> 00:01:39,434
<i>I'm sorry, Ryosuke.</i>

23
00:01:39,434 --> 00:01:41,828
Can I head back to the office?

24
00:01:42,849 --> 00:01:44,082
Huh?

25
00:01:44,991 --> 00:01:49,828
I don't want to leave Kashiwagi
to do everything on his own.

26
00:01:51,303 --> 00:01:54,743
Sorry. I know we had plans...

27
00:02:01,636 --> 00:02:02,887
Sure.

28
00:02:04,276 --> 00:02:06,258
I'm fine with it.

29
00:02:07,404 --> 00:02:08,924
Do your best.

30
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:12,371
Thank you.

31
00:02:34,667 --> 00:02:42,699
[Glad to hear that. Rest well!]

32
00:03:39,610 --> 00:03:44,558
Mr. Taguchi, regarding the test results...

33
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:46,310
I'll send the documents.

34
00:03:46,310 --> 00:03:48,259
Thank you so much.

35
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:55,584
Good work yesterday.

36
00:03:56,350 --> 00:04:00,240
Thank you. But I'm really sorry.

37
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,755
No worries. It's work. It can't be helped.

38
00:04:06,216 --> 00:04:07,429
Okay.

39
00:04:08,976 --> 00:04:11,495
Really, don't worry about it.

40
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:20,519
Hey, Ryosuke!

41
00:04:24,381 --> 00:04:28,329
The get-together is today, right?

42
00:04:33,750 --> 00:04:35,263
Yes, it is.

43
00:04:58,524 --> 00:05:00,471
Ms. Yamane.

44
00:05:00,471 --> 00:05:01,884
Yes?

45
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:04,788
Shall we get ready for the get-together?

46
00:05:04,788 --> 00:05:06,448
Got it.

47
00:05:15,696 --> 00:05:17,029
So?

48
00:05:18,229 --> 00:05:19,456
Well?

49
00:05:20,167 --> 00:05:22,258
Did something happen with him?

50
00:05:24,366 --> 00:05:27,323
I have time to talk now if you want.

51
00:05:31,143 --> 00:05:33,010
Well...

52
00:05:35,817 --> 00:05:40,449
"Don't worry about it", huh?

53
00:05:41,349 --> 00:05:46,311
I feel like he's not telling me
how he really feels.

54
00:05:50,055 --> 00:05:53,085
I don't want to force it out of him.

55
00:05:54,272 --> 00:05:56,724
Did you tell her the truth?

56
00:05:56,724 --> 00:05:58,925
I didn't tell her...

57
00:06:00,576 --> 00:06:02,251
and I don't want to.

58
00:06:02,251 --> 00:06:03,918
Huh?

59
00:06:04,671 --> 00:06:07,050
I don't want to trouble her.

60
00:06:18,402 --> 00:06:22,850
What if you hug him tight and comfort him?

61
00:06:24,484 --> 00:06:26,439
Hug him tight?

62
00:06:26,439 --> 00:06:31,950
I mean... A tight hug, then gentle pats.

63
00:06:37,431 --> 00:06:42,788
It's easier to speak your true feelings
if you feel loved.

64
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,622
I see.

65
00:06:57,276 --> 00:06:59,152
- Hug.
- Hug.

66
00:06:59,985 --> 00:07:01,805
Pat, pat.

67
00:07:01,805 --> 00:07:03,820
Pat, pat.

68
00:07:05,248 --> 00:07:07,719
Horizontal? No, vertical.

69
00:07:07,719 --> 00:07:09,449
Like this.

70
00:07:09,449 --> 00:07:14,834
So, our project has more members,
and we can see new phases ahead.

71
00:07:14,834 --> 00:07:17,163
Let's keep pushing forward from here.

72
00:07:17,163 --> 00:07:18,199
Cheers!

73
00:07:18,199 --> 00:07:20,586
Cheers!

74
00:07:31,055 --> 00:07:33,209
Mr. Taguchi, you live in the city, right?

75
00:07:33,209 --> 00:07:34,567
Yes, that's right.

76
00:07:34,567 --> 00:07:35,817
- Wow.
- Good work.

77
00:07:35,817 --> 00:07:37,901
Isn't commuting every day tough?

78
00:07:37,901 --> 00:07:41,730
Not really. It's only about an hour.

79
00:07:46,213 --> 00:07:47,999
Ms. Yamane.

80
00:07:47,999 --> 00:07:49,312
Yes?

81
00:07:49,966 --> 00:07:52,972
I heard you were classmates with Kashiwagi?

82
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:54,752
That's correct.

83
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,560
Were you close?

84
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:01,227
Well, we were on committees together.

85
00:08:01,227 --> 00:08:04,776
And now you happen to work together.

86
00:08:04,776 --> 00:08:08,572
It feels like fate, doesn't it?

87
00:08:08,572 --> 00:08:11,947
Did you date before?

88
00:08:11,947 --> 00:08:13,627
No, I didn't.

89
00:08:14,465 --> 00:08:16,379
I didn't have any luck.

90
00:08:16,379 --> 00:08:20,372
Really? But you're so outgoing,
you must have been popular!

91
00:08:20,372 --> 00:08:22,083
I think so too.

92
00:08:22,083 --> 00:08:24,798
You two should go on a date together.

93
00:08:24,798 --> 00:08:27,484
Mr. Yamamoto, that's enough.

94
00:08:27,484 --> 00:08:29,071
I'll give you a red card.

95
00:08:29,071 --> 00:08:32,991
- What?
- Yeah, Ms. Yamane is uncomfortable.

96
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,799
Hello, it's Taguchi.

97
00:08:59,799 --> 00:09:02,926
<i>Hello. Can you talk now?</i>

98
00:09:02,926 --> 00:09:05,359
Yes, it's fine.

99
00:09:06,294 --> 00:09:10,216
<i>You see, the client insists strongly.</i>

100
00:09:11,251 --> 00:09:15,908
<i>I feel bad asking you to step away
from your current work, but...</i>

101
00:09:23,856 --> 00:09:25,682
Ryosuke.

102
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:31,645
I figured you'd be here.

103
00:09:33,391 --> 00:09:34,818
I see.

104
00:10:04,321 --> 00:10:05,580
Huh?

105
00:10:06,899 --> 00:10:11,576
It's... a way to show affection.

106
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:15,014
Sorry, I took you by surprise.

107
00:10:17,829 --> 00:10:19,302
It's fine.

108
00:10:23,451 --> 00:10:26,963
Are you free on your next day off?

109
00:10:26,963 --> 00:10:30,873
I was hoping we could
spend some quiet time together.

110
00:10:32,844 --> 00:10:34,291
Oh...

111
00:10:35,747 --> 00:10:40,282
Things have been really busy lately.

112
00:10:42,629 --> 00:10:44,177
I see.

113
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,815
That's totally fine.

114
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:56,133
Okay, then.

115
00:10:56,917 --> 00:10:58,552
I'll reach out again.

116
00:10:59,851 --> 00:11:01,151
Okay.

117
00:11:17,183 --> 00:11:20,069
What's your class doing?

118
00:11:20,789 --> 00:11:22,216
A haunted house.

119
00:11:22,216 --> 00:11:23,789
Wow, that sounds fun.

120
00:11:23,789 --> 00:11:25,954
- She's close with Taguchi.
- Ours is a planetarium.

121
00:11:25,954 --> 00:11:28,324
But she seems so gentle.

122
00:11:29,507 --> 00:11:31,098
You're too loud.

123
00:11:32,131 --> 00:11:34,022
Come over when it's open.

124
00:11:34,022 --> 00:11:36,652
I'll go check out your class too.

125
00:11:38,165 --> 00:11:39,966
- What was that?
- Is it a fight?

126
00:11:39,966 --> 00:11:41,757
Oh, man!

127
00:11:45,873 --> 00:11:47,533
Taguchi.

128
00:11:55,343 --> 00:11:56,916
What's wrong?

129
00:12:00,561 --> 00:12:03,401
Hey! What are you guys doing?

130
00:12:03,401 --> 00:12:05,548
Where are you going?

131
00:12:24,603 --> 00:12:27,876
Two is greater than zero.

132
00:12:27,876 --> 00:12:33,806
That means this parabola opens upwards.

133
00:12:33,806 --> 00:12:39,500
And a parabola opening upwards
extends forever upward,

134
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:42,452
so it has a minimum point.

135
00:13:03,283 --> 00:13:04,856
Taguchi.

136
00:13:08,490 --> 00:13:11,809
Are you all right from earlier?

137
00:13:22,186 --> 00:13:24,159
I heard there are rumors.

138
00:13:25,357 --> 00:13:26,657
Huh?

139
00:13:28,127 --> 00:13:32,388
That I'm forcing you to be with me.

140
00:13:38,072 --> 00:13:39,785
It's annoying.

141
00:13:47,367 --> 00:13:49,415
But...

142
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:56,465
Those rumors will die down soon.

143
00:13:58,975 --> 00:14:05,775
I want to keep hanging out with you, Taguchi.

144
00:14:07,086 --> 00:14:08,399
Those rumors aren't...

145
00:14:08,399 --> 00:14:10,366
It bothers me!

146
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:22,540
Don't talk to me anymore.

147
00:14:29,948 --> 00:14:32,636
You can easily make other friends.

148
00:14:37,269 --> 00:14:38,822
See you.

149
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:51,862
Okay, let's proceed with this plan.

150
00:14:51,862 --> 00:14:53,724
- Got it.
- Okay.

151
00:14:56,169 --> 00:14:59,574
Oh, by the way, it's a bit sudden,

152
00:14:59,574 --> 00:15:03,063
but Mr. Taguchi is leaving the project.

153
00:15:03,063 --> 00:15:05,116
What?

154
00:15:05,116 --> 00:15:08,006
Our client apparently has their reasons.

155
00:15:09,098 --> 00:15:12,434
Sorry, could you handle the paperwork?

156
00:15:13,858 --> 00:15:15,178
Okay.

157
00:15:37,401 --> 00:15:39,202
Hey.

158
00:15:43,191 --> 00:15:44,678
Hey.

159
00:15:50,851 --> 00:15:55,370
I heard you're moving
to a new company next week.

160
00:16:02,830 --> 00:16:04,223
Yeah.

161
00:16:08,657 --> 00:16:10,816
That must be tough.

162
00:16:12,267 --> 00:16:16,042
I feel like you have to learn so much.

163
00:16:18,205 --> 00:16:19,888
Well...

164
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:23,202
Yeah, I guess.

165
00:16:29,148 --> 00:16:30,815
Hey.

166
00:16:33,460 --> 00:16:35,284
This transfer...

167
00:16:36,209 --> 00:16:38,656
It was decided suddenly, right?

168
00:16:45,550 --> 00:16:46,983
I'm sorry.

169
00:17:01,597 --> 00:17:03,858
Ryosuke,

170
00:17:05,449 --> 00:17:11,236
you always value how I feel.

171
00:17:14,362 --> 00:17:19,051
You always worry about whether I'm upset.

172
00:17:19,663 --> 00:17:22,258
And you're so considerate.

173
00:17:27,005 --> 00:17:31,584
But I'm not sure if you're being honest

174
00:17:31,584 --> 00:17:35,613
about your own feelings.

175
00:17:36,552 --> 00:17:38,442
I'm worried.

176
00:17:45,584 --> 00:17:47,249
I...

177
00:17:48,314 --> 00:17:54,435
want to be someone you can talk honestly to

178
00:17:54,435 --> 00:17:56,515
about this stuff.

179
00:17:58,854 --> 00:18:00,779
Even if...

180
00:18:01,617 --> 00:18:05,244
I'm not dependable enough.

181
00:18:15,341 --> 00:18:16,676
Yeah.

182
00:18:19,673 --> 00:18:21,159
Thank you.

183
00:18:27,065 --> 00:18:28,526
But...

184
00:18:33,299 --> 00:18:36,236
You don't need to worry about anything.

185
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:47,293
What?

186
00:18:47,293 --> 00:18:50,632
You made her say all that and then ran away?
That's embarrassing.

187
00:18:50,632 --> 00:18:52,205
Shut up.

188
00:18:53,941 --> 00:18:57,631
Just tell her everything already.

189
00:18:57,631 --> 00:19:00,699
You're just making things messier
by hiding it.

190
00:19:01,908 --> 00:19:03,617
I know, but...

191
00:19:06,338 --> 00:19:09,948
Get a grip! You're dating her!

192
00:19:19,695 --> 00:19:22,183
Putting distance between you again...

193
00:19:22,866 --> 00:19:25,499
Are you gonna regret it for years again?

194
00:19:35,657 --> 00:19:37,810
I want to see Yamane.

195
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:44,680
Okay, okay. Just have some water.

196
00:19:45,606 --> 00:19:47,661
I really miss her.

197
00:19:51,646 --> 00:19:53,735
What about a class reunion?

198
00:19:54,361 --> 00:19:56,694
I'd never get invited.

199
00:19:58,615 --> 00:20:00,779
Find her on social media.

200
00:20:05,375 --> 00:20:07,108
You looked her up, huh?

201
00:20:07,755 --> 00:20:09,501
I couldn't find her.

202
00:20:09,501 --> 00:20:12,914
Ew, creepy.

203
00:20:12,914 --> 00:20:15,505
Shut up.

204
00:20:18,188 --> 00:20:23,288
It's not like you'll never see her again.

205
00:20:23,921 --> 00:20:25,980
So work on yourself instead.

206
00:20:36,553 --> 00:20:38,300
Don't fall asleep.

207
00:20:48,534 --> 00:20:50,548
When Shiori...

208
00:20:53,962 --> 00:20:56,754
and I make eye contact,

209
00:20:57,453 --> 00:21:00,668
I love that smile she gives me.

210
00:21:03,852 --> 00:21:09,543
I worry a little when she falls asleep
right after drinking, though...

211
00:21:10,636 --> 00:21:13,451
But I love that side too.

212
00:21:17,572 --> 00:21:20,142
I love it when she calls my name.

213
00:21:23,971 --> 00:21:27,291
I love how unexpectedly bold she is.

214
00:21:35,004 --> 00:21:38,450
I could go on forever
about all the things I like.

215
00:21:49,008 --> 00:21:51,096
I want to be with her forever.

216
00:21:54,415 --> 00:21:57,451
Tell her that. Say it to her face.

217
00:21:58,773 --> 00:22:01,164
Stop trying to act cool.

218
00:23:07,366 --> 00:23:10,639
<i>In the end, we never got to
talk it through properly.</i>

219
00:23:21,386 --> 00:23:23,687
<i>Ryosuke, once again...</i>

220
00:23:25,599 --> 00:23:27,789
<i>disappeared.</i>

221
00:23:30,327 --> 00:23:33,327
Are things going well with Yamane?

222
00:23:33,327 --> 00:23:34,988
I want you to give this back.

223
00:23:34,988 --> 00:23:37,581
I'll be waiting to hear about it.

224
00:23:37,581 --> 00:23:40,067
I wanted to protect Shiori.

225
00:23:40,067 --> 00:23:43,663
Did I do something to make him hate me?

226
00:23:43,663 --> 00:23:48,670
Maybe it'd be good for you two
to trust yourselves.

227
00:23:49,326 --> 00:23:51,012
Ryosuke.

228
00:23:51,012 --> 00:23:53,619
I'm sorry. I'm so pathetic.

229
00:23:53,619 --> 00:23:56,260
It's okay to show that side of you.

230
00:23:56,260 --> 00:24:00,673
I'm so glad we got to meet again.
